From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksandr Tyshchenko <oleksandr_tyshchenko@epam.com>
Date: Fri, 15 Jul 2022 11:20:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] xen-bus: Set offline if backend's state is XenbusStateClosed

Both state (XenbusStateClosed) and online (0) are expected by
toolstack/xl devd to completely destroy the device. But "offline" is
never being set by the backend resulting in timeout during domain
destruction, garbage in Xestore and still running Qemu instance.

(cherry picked from commit 20b5702efd9ca805e1c28dd5a861639518b8b696)

Signed-off-by: Oleksandr Tyshchenko <oleksandr_tyshchenko@epam.com>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [downstream fork / BSP-layer delta; not submitted upstream]
Origin: https://github.com/xen-troops/qemu commit 20b5702efd9ca805e1c28dd5a861639518b8b696
---
 hw/xen/xen-bus.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/xen/xen-bus.c b/hw/xen/xen-bus.c
index 181c9b093..ff19fff71 100644
--- a/hw/xen/xen-bus.c
+++ b/hw/xen/xen-bus.c
@@ -525,6 +525,9 @@ static void xen_device_backend_changed(void *opaque, const char *path)
         xen_device_backend_set_state(xendev, XenbusStateClosed);
     }
 
+    if (xen_device_backend_get_state(xendev) == XenbusStateClosed)
+        xen_device_backend_set_online(xendev, false);
+
     /*
      * If a backend is still 'online' then we should leave it alone but,
      * if a backend is not 'online', then the device is a candidate
